{
 "_doc": "What must not be left after the port (read by residue_scan.py). level: block = the gate fails while it remains (unless waived); warn = review, may be acceptable; info = context. where: code (.cs/.vb), markup (.cshtml, .razor, .aspx, .ascx, .master, .asmx, .svc, .ashx, .asax; code rules apply), static (.html, .htm, .js under wwwroot; code rules apply), project (.csproj, .vbproj, .fsproj, .props, .targets), config (.config, appsettings*.json), sql (string literals in code that look like SQL, and .sql files; scope \"line\" = the whole line holding such a literal, for concatenation), file (the file's name or path). when: always, postgresql (only when the database target is PostgreSQL only), dual (only with a dual-database target), postgresql|dual (both). scope \"file\": one regex over the whole file, multi-line; the hit is the line where the match starts. requires_file / unless_file: the rule applies only to files where the regex matches / does not match. info_if_tree: the rule reports at info level when a project or props file in the scanned folder matches (for example a CoreWCF package reference). playbook = the dotnet-modernization playbook that fixes it; kb = DevTx knowledge-base files. group: port = residue of the .NET Framework port; linux = Linux readiness (also run alone with --only linux for applications already on modern .NET).",
 "rules": [
  {
   "id": "PROJ-LEGACY",
   "where": "project",
   "level": "block",
   "pattern": "<Project\\s+ToolsVersion=|<TargetFrameworkVersion>v4",
   "message": "Legacy (non SDK-style) project file or .NET Framework target",
   "playbook": "build-and-packages",
   "kb": [
    "01"
   ],
   "group": [
    "port"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "PROJ-NETFX-TFM",
   "where": "project",
   "level": "block",
   "pattern": "<TargetFrameworks?>[^<]*\\bnet4\\d",
   "message": ".NET Framework target framework still listed",
   "playbook": "build-and-packages",
   "kb": [
    "01"
   ],
   "group": [
    "port"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "PROJ-PACKAGES-CONFIG",
   "where": "file",
   "level": "block",
   "pattern": "(^|/)packages\\.config$",
   "message": "packages.config still present (use PackageReference)",
   "playbook": "build-and-packages",
   "kb": [
    "01",
    "06"
   ],
   "group": [
    "port"
   ]
  },
  {
